title: Left-wing Split
new-page: true 
subtitle: The Left's disagreements with our policies have grown too severe.
tags: event
view-if: left_dissent >= 60
on-arrival: left_split = 1; left_strength = left_strength/2; workers_rsdrp -= 5; unemployed_rsdrp -= 5; workers_other += 5; workers_rkp += 3; n_advisors -= 1 if levi_advisor == 1; levi_advisor = 0; rb_strength -= 300; rkp_relation -= 5; rb_militancy -= 0.05 if rb_militancy >= 0.1; n_advisors -= 1 if seydewitz_advisor == 1; seydewitz_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1 if rosenfeld_advisor == 1; rosenfeld_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1 if siemsen_advisor == 1; siemsen_advisor = 0
max-visits: 1

= Left-wing members split

Our policy choices have greatly offended the left, and many of their leaders have split to form a new party, the RSRPI, or the Socialist Worker's Party of Internationalists. They do not count a huge section of our membership, so this should be survivable. [? if centrists_resign = 1 : Many former Centrist Marxists have joined with the RSRPI, the party formed by dissident leftists. They have brought their support base and organization skills to the party, leading to its growth as a nascent rival to the RSDRP for the support of the working class. ?]

- @centrist: The Center, represented by Martov and Axelrod, win out once again, perhaps their message of compromise and unity will keep the party from fracturing further.
- @labor: The Unions emerge victorious, their practical, worker-focused messaging will surely win back lost voters!
- @reform: With no counterweight to hold them back, the Reformists and Liquidationists of the Party manage to exert their influence, calling for the preservation the Republic against monarchist and radical voices, expanding the party's electorate, and expanded cooperation with democratic parties, bourgeois or otherwise.
- @marxghost: There are no factions left to compete for power within the Party.

@centrist
choose-if: centrists_resign = 0
unavailable-subtitle: Our Centrist wing has since left the party.
on-arrival: ideology = "centrist"; center_strength += 10; center_dissent -= 10; left_dissent -= 5; reformist_dissent -= 5
go-to: rsrpi_formed if centrists_resign = 1 and not rsrpi_formed

We have adopted Centrist rhetoric.

@labor
choose-if: unions_independent = 0
on-arrival: ideology = "labor"; labor_strength += 10; wtb_support += 1; labor_dissent -= 5; rkp_relation -= 3
go-to: rsrpi_formed if centrists_resign = 1 and not rsrpi_formed

We have adopted Labor-centric rhetoric.

@reform
choose-if: rdp_formed = 0
unavailable-subtitle: Our reformist wing has since left the party.
on-arrival: ideology = "reformist"; reformist_strength += 10; democratization += 1; reformist_dissent -= 5; z_relation += 5; kadets_relation += 5; rkp_relation -= 8; moderate_plan_support += 1
go-to: rsrpi_formed if centrists_resign = 1 and not rsrpi_formed

We have adopted Reformist rhetoric.

@marxghost
subtitle: Using the power of Enlightened Centrism, Kautskyism, and the sheer willpower of the few remaining in our party, Martov summons the Spirit of Karl Marx himself to save Russian Socialism.
unavailable-subtitle: There has to be at least one faction in the Party that can still lead us, right? Right, Tovarisch Martov? Tovarisch Martov... are you there?
view-if: reformists_resign = 1 and unions_independent = 1 and centrists_resign = 1
on-arrival: ideology = "partydeath"
go-to: rsrpi_formed if centrists_resign = 1 and not rsrpi_formed

How did we get here, Tovarisch?